NAR Lifecycle

	The NAR lifecycle copies the default Maven lifecycle and adds native goals to its phases.
The table below shows the different phases of the NAR Lifecycle and the goals (including
standard maven goals) attached to them. The order is left to right, top to bottom.

*------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
| <Phase>                | <Goals (NAR Goals in bold)>                                         |
*------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------+ 
| validate               | <<nar-validate>>                                                    |
*------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------+ 
| initialize             | <<nar-download>>                                                    |
*------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------+ 
| generate-sources       | <<nar-unpack>>, <<nar-test-unpack>>                                 |
*------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------+ 
| process-sources        | <<nar-gnu-configure>>, <<nar-include-path>>, <<nar-test-include-path>>|
*------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------+ 
| generate-resources     | <<nar-system-generate>>                             |
*------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------+ 
| process-resources      | resources, <<nar-resources>>, <<nar-gnu-resources>>                 |
*------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------+ 
| compile                | compile, <<nar-gnu-make>>, <<nar-compile>>           |
*------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------+ 
| process-classes        | <<nar-gnu-process>>, <<nar-process-libraries>>                      |
*------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------+ 
| generate-test-sources  |                                                                     |
*------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------+ 
| process-test-sources   |                                                                     |
*------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------+ 
| generate-test-resources|                                                                     |
*------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------+ 
| process-test-resources | testResources                                                       |
*------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------+ 
| test-compile           | testCompile, <<nar-testCompile>>                                    |
*------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------+ 
| process-test-classes   |                                                                     |
*------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------+ 
| test                   | test, <<nar-test>>                                                  |
*------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------+ 
| prepare-package        | <<nar-prepare-package>>                                             |
*------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------+ 
| package                | <<nar-package>>, jar                                                |
*------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------+ 
| pre-integration-test   |                                                                     |
*------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------+ 
| integration-test       | integration-test                                                    |
*------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------+ 
| post-integration-test  |                                                                     |
*------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------+ 
| verify                 |                                                                     |
*------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------+ 
| install                | install                                                             |
*------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------+ 
| deploy                 | deploy                                                              |
*------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------+ 


	The NAR plugin attaches the nar files it produces to the main artifact (jar) so the standard
install and deploy plugins of maven do their job.

	The nar-assembly goal is not part of the lifestyle and should be called independently.

Compilation Database

	<<nar-compile>> and <<nar-testCompile>> write <<<target/compile_commands.json>>>, the
JSON compilation database that clangd, clang-tidy and the SonarQube C/C++ analyzer read
to learn how each source file is compiled: its working directory, its whole command
line and its object file. It always goes in the build directory of the module, never
next to the sources, and there is nothing to configure.

	Both goals write to the same file, so it holds the library and the test sources
together; each compilation replaces its own entries and keeps the others. Every source
the task knows how to compile gets an entry, not only those it recompiles, so an
incremental build leaves the database as complete as a clean one. Only C and C++
sources are recorded: a Windows resource compiled with windres is not.

Include Path Goals

	The <<nar-include-path>> and <<nar-test-include-path>> goals publish the include
directories the sources compile against, so that an IDE can resolve the headers of a
project that <does not compile yet>. Each writes a plain list (<<<nar-include-path.txt>>>),
a Visual Studio Code C/C++ configuration (<<<c_cpp_properties.json>>>) and a project
property (<<<nar.include.path>>>, and <<<nar.include.path.test>>> for the tests); the
main-scope files go to target/nar and the test-scope ones to target/test-nar.

	[[1]] <<They run before compile, both of them.>> The test pair is bound next to the
	main one: <<nar-test-unpack>> in generate-sources and <<nar-test-include-path>> in
	process-sources. generate-test-sources and process-test-sources come after compile
	in the standard lifecycle, so binding them there would make the test include path
	unreachable without compiling the module first. <<<mvn process-sources>>> therefore
	yields both configurations.

	Running earlier has a price: a plain <<<mvn compile>>> now reaches the test unpack.
	<<nar-test-unpack>> honours <<<skipTests>>>, like <<nar-testCompile>> and
	<<nar-test>>, so <<<-DskipTests>>> or <<<-Dmaven.test.skip=true>>> leave the test
	dependencies packed.

	[[2]] <<They are self-sufficient on their own.>> They can be called directly from the
	command line (<<<mvn nar:nar-include-path nar:nar-test-include-path>>>) on a module
	that has just been cleaned. Whether they unpack the dependencies themselves is
	decided by <<<nar.includePath.unpack>>>:

		* unset, the default: they unpack only when something is missing, that is, when a
		dependency declares a <<<noarch>>> NAR in its nar.properties (where the headers
		travel) and its directory is not there. Inside a build, where the unpack goals
		have already run, this costs nothing.

		* true: they always unpack.

		* false: they never unpack.

		[]

	Whatever is still missing is reported with a warning naming the dependencies left
	out, instead of being dropped silently: an incomplete include path is worse than
	none, because the IDE resolves some headers and flags the others as missing.

	[]
	
	
